<spell-notebook "slider theming">
	<header level="1">
		Slider
		<header>A slider allows users to select values within a range.</>
	</>
	<slider-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the family's tokens, live, plus how to set them and which themes touch it. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			Theme with the public `--ui-slider-*` tokens: set one on the element, on any ancestor (`:root` included), or on
			the slider's box through `::part(slider)`. They inherit into the shadow root, where the sheet reads each through
			a private alias, so nothing inside blocks them. Style the pieces with `::part()`: `track`, `track-fill`,
			`thumb`, `labels` and `label`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-slider {
			  --ui-slider-track-height: 0.25em;
			}
			ui-slider::part(thumb) {
			  box-shadow: none;
			}
			```
		</>
		<message state="info" size="small">
			<markdown>
				`inverted` swaps in its own `--ui-slider-inverted-*` colours; `color` replaces `--ui-slider-fill-color`; a size
				scales the whole slider (every length is `em`). Never set the `--_ui-*` / `--_slider-*` names: they're the sheet's private
				plumbing (the element writes the thumb and label positions there).
			</>
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-slider" playground>
				<ui-slider value="5" aria-label="Volume"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>The theme menu in the header (Spell, Glass, Fruity, Merlot, Paper, Midnight, Crisp, Pop, Matrix) changes the colours a slider inherits.</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
